m/repos/django/asgiref/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/deployments","created_at":"2015-12-23T17:07:13Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T00:24:22Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-10T18:42:14Z","git_url":"git://github.com/django/asgiref.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:django/asgiref.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/django/asgiref.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/django/asgiref","homepage":"https://asgi.readthedocs.io/en/latest/","size":584,"stargazers_count":1600,"watchers_count":1600,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":232,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":59,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":232,"open_issues":59,"watchers":1600,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/pulls/286","html_url":"https://github.com/django/asgiref/pull/286","diff_url":"https://github.com/django/asgiref/pull/286.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/django/asgiref/pull/286.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Hi folks! We very happily use `asgiref` in @mitmproxy since the last release, thank you very much for your work here. 😃🍰 \r\n\r\nFollowing a bug report where a user's Flask app (wrapped with asgiref) did not see request bodies (https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4717), I discovered that Flask expects a content-length header to be set, as it doesn't trust `wsgi.input` to have read-until-EOF semantics. This then fails for chunked request bodies and no body is read at all.\r\n\r\nTo demonstrate this, here's a self-contained example with asgiref+Flask:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport asyncio\r\n\r\nimport asgiref.wsgi\r\nfrom flask import Flask, request\r\n\r\napp = Flask(__name__)\r\n\r\n@app.route('/', methods=['GET', 'POST'])\r\ndef hello_world():\r\n    return f\"{request.data=}\"\r\n\r\nasgi_app = asgiref.wsgi.WsgiToAsgi(app)\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    scope = {\r\n        \"type\": \"http\",\r\n        \"asgi\": {\r\n            \"version\": \"3.0\",\r\n            \"spec_version\": \"2.1\",\r\n        },\r\n        \"http_version\": \"1.1\",\r\n        \"method\": \"POST\",\r\n        \"scheme\": \"http\",\r\n        \"path\": \"/\",\r\n        \"raw_path\": b\"/\",\r\n        \"query_string\": b\"\",\r\n        \"headers\": [[b\"transfer-encoding\", b\"chunked\"]],\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    async def receive():\r\n        return {\r\n            \"type\": \"http.request\",\r\n            \"body\": b\"Hello world\",\r\n        }\r\n\r\n    async def send(data):\r\n        print(f\"send {data=}\")\r\n        \r\n    asyncio.run(asgi_app(scope, receive, send))\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\n```\r\nsend data={'type': 'http.response.start', 'status': 200, 'headers': [(b'content-type', b'text/html; charset=utf-8'), (b'content-length', b'16')]}\r\nsend data={'type': 'http.response.body', 'body': b\"request.data=b''\", 'more_body': True}\r\nsend data={'type': 'http.response.body'}\r\n```\r\n\r\nObserve in the second line that there's no request data. The fix here seems to be to signal to WSGI apps that read-until-EOF semantics actually *do* exist by setting `wsgi.input_terminated` (proposed in https://gist.github.com/mitsuhiko/5721547). This PR simply does that and adds a test for it.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/issues/286/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/asgiref/issues/286/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/comments/892744636","html_url":"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4717#issuecomment-892744636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4717","id":892744636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAAfumM41NjO8","user":{"login":"mhils","id":1019198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTkxOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1019198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils","html_url":"https://github.com/mhils","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/subscriptions","organizati